<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Donation of Constantine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Constitutum Constantini</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Donation of Constantine is a forged Roman imperial decree, probably composed in the eighth century, in which the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-i">Constantine the Great</a> appears to grant Pope Sylvester I and his successors authority over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and the western half of the empire. Used to support papal claims throughout the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, it was shown to be a forgery by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorenzo-valla">Lorenzo Valla</a> in 1440.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/donation-of-constantine.jpg" alt="Donation of Constantine" width="320" height="206" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown medieval artist in Rome · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sylvester_I_and_Constantine.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
